[00:23.74]1. Here with us are aged ones,
[00:31.02]Those whose youth has passed.
[00:38.36]Here among us they endure;
[00:44.22]Still they’re holding fast.
[00:52.40]Loss of strength besets them all;
[00:58.62]Loss of mates for some.
[01:07.60]Father, please confirm their faith
[01:14.82]In the life to come.
[01:22.10](Chorus)
[01:22.10]Father, you remember
[01:27.60]How in faith they’ve run.
[01:36.32]Give them your assurance;
[01:43.38]May they hear, “Well done!”
[02:45.80]2. Splendid is gray-headedness
[02:52.86]Found in ways of right.
[03:01.02]Beautiful are faithful ones
[03:09.13]In Jehovah’s sight.
[03:13.37]May we always recognize
[03:20.52]They were once young too.
[03:29.43]Loyally they gave their best
[03:34.95]When their strength was new.
[03:43.77](Chorus)
[03:44.03]Father, you remember
[03:49.43]How in faith they’ve run.
[03:58.33]Give them your assurance;
[04:05.59]May they hear, “Well done!”
